  "id": "paradoxical-thinking",
  "term": "paradoxical thinking",
  "definition": "Paradoxical thinking is the ability to recognize, accept, and actively work with opposing demands or requirements. In leadership or team settings, it means approaching conflicting goals, such as maintaining high performance while also encouraging innovation, in an inclusive and tolerant way.",
